CADzilla licensing
==================

Copyright (C) 2026 Todd Houg

CADzilla is open hardware with open software. The repository is under
two licenses, according to what each part is:

  Hardware   CERN Open Hardware Licence Version 2 - Permissive
             (SPDX: CERN-OHL-P-2.0), full text in LICENSES/CERN-OHL-P-2.0.txt

  Software   GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
             later version (SPDX: GPL-3.0-or-later), full text in
             LICENSES/GPL-3.0.txt

Source files carry an SPDX-License-Identifier line naming their license.
Files that cannot carry one (KiCad files, Gerbers, fuse maps, images, PDFs,
disk images and the like) are covered by the table below.


Which license covers what
-------------------------

CERN-OHL-P-2.0 (hardware):
  schematics/                  KiCad schematics, PCB layout, libraries,
                               Gerbers, fabrication outputs, BOM (.csv/.xls)
  pld/                         GAL16V8 logic equations (src/), test vectors
                               and assembled fuse maps (jed/)
  docs/cadzilla-manual.pdf     the CADzilla User Reference Manual
  docs/images/cadzilla.png     the board image
  docs/design/                 hardware design notes

GPL-3.0-or-later (software):
  software/                    every program and library: czgfx, cz88gfx,
                               czbasic, the GSX driver ddcz and the example
                               programs, with their sources, build scripts,
                               tests, BASIC demos and releases
  tools/                       build, release and emulator support scripts
                               (including tools/mkmanual.py, the generator
                               of docs/cadzilla-manual.pdf)
  tests/                       emulator test programs and expected output
  .claude/                     AI-assistance skills and scaffolding script
  docs/czgfx-guide.pdf, docs/cz88gfx-guide.pdf, docs/czbasic-manual.pdf
                               the software guides
  docs/images/czgfx/, docs/images/cz88gfx/
                               screenshots of the demo programs
  README.md, CLAUDE.md, other top-level notes

A program that links the czgfx or cz88gfx library, or is built from
CADzilla software, is a work based on GPL-licensed code and is covered by
the GPL as a whole.


Third-party material (not covered by either license)
----------------------------------------------------

These files are included for reference or to run the toolchains. They
remain the property of their owners and are under their owners' terms:

  docs/datasheets/             manufacturers' datasheets and manuals (Hitachi,
                               Brooktree, Texas Instruments, Fairchild,
                               Lattice, Infineon/Cypress) and the Markdown
                               transcriptions made of them

  CP/M disk images (*.DSK):
    tools/altairsim/pristine/CPM22SYS.DSK, tools/altairsim/pristine/EMPTY.DSK,
    software/m80/czgfx/releases/CZGFXLIB-*.DSK,
    software/m80/czbasic/demodisk/CZBDEMO.DSK
                               These contain Digital Research CP/M 2.2 and its
                               utilities, and DRI's RMAC, LINK, LIB and XREF,
                               distributed under the July 2022 grant by
                               DRDOS, Inc. (http://www.cpm.z80.de/license.html).
                               CPM22SYS.DSK also carries Microsoft MACRO-80
                               (M80, L80, LIB80, CREF80) and a MicroPro
                               International program, which remain under
                               their owners' copyrights. The CADzilla files
                               on these disks (czgfx, czbasic) are
                               GPL-3.0-or-later.

See tools/altairsim/upstream/README.md for the provenance of the
third-party CP/M tools, and for GSX-80 and the other tools that are kept
out of the repository.


